UPDATE "gaps" SET "description" = 'REST-LANDING LIMITS STATED AS RISE HAVE NO PARAMETER. Parameter 12 is the horizontal run between landings (TERM-091), and its scope note keeps it distinct from the vertical dimension. Admitted codes state the same rest-landing requirement as a vertical figure instead of, or beside, a run: REF-01012 TEK17 12-16(2) (rest plane per height difference, no landing run stated), REF-00987 ADA 405.6 (rise for any ramp run), REF-00992 para 1.26(c) and Table 1''s ''Maximum rise'' column, REF-00995 Art. 19 para 4. A rise cannot be filed under parameter 12 without mixing two dimensions in one value space, and a run cannot be inferred from a rise without the gradient. Figures are not copied here (rule 5); they are in the persisted payloads (retrieval-log/session_2026-10-30-rest-landing-parameter/) at those clauses. Run, going and landing figures for other codes already sit under parameter 3 inside claimed_unit strings (derive: select extraction_id, ref_id, claimed_unit from source_value_extractions where parameter_id = 3 and (claimed_unit like ''%run%'' or claimed_unit like ''%going%'' or claimed_unit like ''%projection%'' or claimed_unit like ''%landing%'')); whoever settles the rise question also decides whether those are re-pointed at parameter 12 by new rows (committed rows are immutable, rule 3). OPTIONS, the owner''s call because it fixes what a determination is keyed on: (a) promote TERM-090 level difference. Weakness: TERM-090 is the TOTAL rise a ramp must overcome, and Art. 19 para 1''s bands (parameter 3 rows for REF-00995) already use it as total rise, so a per-flight rise would share a key with the total. (b) mint a term for the rise of a single flight between landings, distinct from the total (RECOMMENDED: the quantity differs, so it is not the near-duplicate the parameter 3 note warns of). (c) one rest-landing parameter with two expressions (needs a unit-class column the schema does not have). The owner''s 2026-10-30 approval (D18/E7) is not recorded in references/project-standards.md; record it when this is settled. || CORRECTED 2026-11-28: Another code in the same shape: REF-00990 (Japan, Cabinet Order 379/2006) Article 19 para 2 item 4 ハ states the landing as a rise, with a tread, and a gradient exemption elsewhere in the same article; read 2026-11-28 (observation 99, targeted scan of parameter 12), figures at that clause in retrieval-log/session_2026-11-20-core-work/a4390f9b6c346623.xml, corroborated by MLIT''s 2021 design standard (retrieval-log/session_2026-11-28-research-lang-jur-first-run/e63bd38e6b233497.pdf pp. 28, 29, 34). Not a parameter 12 row; same decision as the codes above.', "updated_at" = '2026-11-28 01:32', "updated_by_session" = 'session_2026-11-28-research-lang-jur-first-run' WHERE "gap_id" = 'GAP-070';

